From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThaRae <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compositor: Release cached rasters of contexts that stop
 painting

A context keeps the rasters of its SVG images and repeated tiles, and
its text blobs, to make its next frame cheap. A context that has stopped
painting may not make one for a long time, so release them once it has
painted nothing for a while: 4 seconds for a hidden context, which
paints nothing until it is shown again, and 30 seconds for a visible
one, which keeps its text blobs, since it may be read for a while and
then scrolled. Each context is timed on its own, so an animation or a
blinking caret in one does not keep the rasters of the others.

Dropping a GPU raster only hands its texture back to Skia's resource
cache, which is trimmed after a flush, and a context that paints nothing
does not flush. So after a release, purge the cache's unlocked scratch
resources and give the allocators' free pages back: mimalloc's on the
main thread, glibc's on a thread of its own, since its trim walks every
arena, and the malloc zones' on macOS.

LADYBIRD_COMPOSITOR_IDLE_RELEASE=0 turns the release off.
LADYBIRD_COMPOSITOR_IDLE_RELEASE_LOG=1 logs each release and how long
it took, and each frame that a context paints.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
